  "title": "Sack of Ilion by Fimbria",
  "summary": "In 85 BCE, during the First Mithridatic War, the rogue Roman commander Gaius Flavius Fimbria besieged, captured, and leveled the historic city of Ilion after its citizens refused him entry and offered surrender to his rival Sulla. Fimbria slaughtered the inhabitants, burned the sanctuary of Athena, and dismantled the city walls. Following Fimbria's defeat, Sulla compensated the surviving Ilians and restored the city, reaffirming Rome's mythic ancestry and ties to Troy.",
